WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.736 --> 00:00:02.610
(gentle music)

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:04.880
- [Woman] Wing on Wo itself being here,

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:08.063
throughout five generations
is a radical act.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.990
And the fact that we're
opening our doors to engage

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.510
with our community in another way,

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:17.060
takes that to the next level.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:19.310
- To bend the word threat.

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:20.143
(clapping)

00:00:20.143 --> 00:00:20.976
- [Mei Lum ] Trying to
integrate a social mission

00:00:20.976 --> 00:00:21.809
into the work that we do here;

00:00:21.809 --> 00:00:26.809
for me it's also cultivating my own

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:30.393
relationship with Chinatown as it changes.

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:33.310
- [Narrator] This Great Big Story

00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:35.830
is brought to you by Delta.

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:37.370
When we venture out into the world,

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.143
we see all that we share.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:52.410
- My name is Mei Lum.

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:54.810
I'm the fifth generation
owner of Wing on Wo

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:57.533
and also the founder and
director of the Wow Project.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:01.330
Wing and Wo is the oldest continually

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:04.040
run store in Chinatown.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:08.430
It was started by my
great-great-grandfather in 1890.

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:13.430
Today Wing on Wo, sells a
collection of porcelain.

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:16.270
Wing on Wo is completely family run.

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:19.060
The store has been throughout the years,

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:20.543
like our family living room.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:23.780
It's where we meet up, where we hang out.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:25.420
There's a kitchen in the back.

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:28.530
We're not only selling porcelain pieces,

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:31.180
but we're also supporting the community

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:33.270
through the work that we
do with the Wow project.

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:36.103
And we're doing that
through arts and activism.

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:43.570
At the time when Chinatown was forming,

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:46.450
we had no other place to go.

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:50.130
We were being pushed out and marginalized,

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:53.670
so we had to in order to
survive, create these Chinatowns,

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:55.033
to pass a safe space.

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:57.870
There's still recent immigrants

00:01:57.870 --> 00:02:02.373
that are coming to America
and needing a space to land.

00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:06.620
But Chinatown's around the country

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:09.710
are at a very pivotal
moment with their longevity

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:12.050
and reassessing their purpose

00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:14.793
in serving these immigrant communities.

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:19.440
A lot of different Asian Americans

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:22.140
who aren't even Chinese, come
to Chinatown to grocery shop

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:25.923
to learn about their
culture and their identity.

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:32.290
For me, the store itself
has been a landing

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:34.740
and launching pad in my life to understand

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:36.690
my Asian-American identity;

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:39.880
to understand Chinese culture and history

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:42.530
as well as my sense of
self and sense of grounding

00:02:42.530 --> 00:02:43.763
in this community.

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:54.730
After I graduated college I
decided to live and work abroad

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:57.030
for eight years.

00:02:57.030 --> 00:03:00.570
I came back hoping to
apply to grad school,

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:03.680
but right before I
hopped on the plane back,

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:05.960
my dad had called me and told me,

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:09.823
we are thinking about selling
the business and the building.

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:15.730
I always had relied on having
this space as a constant.

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:17.790
So when I realized that
this was not going to

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:20.580
be here anymore that's when
you start thinking about,

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:23.163
how can I continue this legacy?

00:03:25.008 --> 00:03:27.860
(melancholic music)

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:30.650
I never ever thought that I
would be taking over the store,

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:33.490
but I started learning
about gentrification

00:03:33.490 --> 00:03:34.460
and displacement.

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:37.590
And that really opened my
eyes to the larger context

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:41.240
that my family situation was existing in.

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:42.440
I had to make that decision,

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:44.440
if I was going to do something about it.

00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:55.250
When I took over I had
a lot of interactions

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:57.810
with all these people
in my community about

00:03:57.810 --> 00:03:58.770
what they care about,

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:02.710
and I was in a position to do something.

00:04:02.710 --> 00:04:05.300
So we started a community initiative

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:08.243
out of the store front
called the Wow Project.

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:11.300
We do host different public programs

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:15.930
in the storefront space, like
screenings, talks, readings.

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:18.500
- It seemed as if there
were serpents and ocean.

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:20.925
I fought to be with my son.

00:04:20.925 --> 00:04:21.758
(clapping)

00:04:21.758 --> 00:04:24.050
- [Mei Lum] We have a
storefront residency program

00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:27.060
that we offer up to an
emerging Asian American artist.

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:29.680
We also have the youth internship program.

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:31.233
It really runs the gamut.

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:37.840
The largest event that we hold

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:39.833
is our anniversary fundraiser.

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:45.640
And we've outgrown the
store, so just to see

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:48.193
how many people came out,
it was really incredible.

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:51.980
Chinatown has been such
a safe haven for me,

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:56.160
and I'm happy that I was
able to grow up in this space

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:57.480
because it's grounding me.

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:00.650
So for me it's amazing to hear
that, that's the same thing

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:01.810
for other folks.

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:03.110
That's the dream right?

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:05.090
- So much of this year has been about

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:07.380
strengthening our community.

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:08.660
So to the Wow team,

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:11.983
thank you for your heart soul
creativity and imagination.

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:16.820
- We want people to be able
to cultivate themselves,

00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:19.210
nurture themselves here
and be able to like do

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:21.910
even bigger and better things beyond this.

00:05:23.560 --> 00:05:26.143
(gentle music)

